+# 512 profile, not 1024: the non-CC collector reserves two spaces of
+# dalvik.vm.heapsize each plus a 64 MB non-moving space, and at 256 MB that is
+# 576 MB of a 32-bit process's address space before anything else is mapped.
+# 128 MB is what let system_server start.  Inheriting the smaller profile
+# rather than overriding the property, because a later
+# PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES of the same key does not win - verified: the
+# override was in golden.mk and build.prop still came out with heapsize=256m.
+$(call inherit-product, frameworks/native/build/phone-hdpi-512-dalvik-heap.mk)
+
+# ART's concurrent copying collector is what makes zygote fail on this handset.
+# Measured on 24-25 August from /proc/<zygote>/maps:
+#   * [anon:dalvik-main space (region space)] reserves 2x the heap - 512 MB of
+#     address space for a 256 MB heap, at a fixed low address
+#   * 477 separate [anon:dalvik-thread local mark stack] mappings, 16 KB each,
+#     scattered across the 2 GB above TASK_UNMAPPED_BASE
+# Only 142 MB is actually mapped up there, but it is cut into 676 holes whose
+# largest is 21.7 MB, so the boot image cannot be placed:
+#   E zygote: Failed anonymous mmap(0x6f643000, 94806016, ...): Out of memory
+#   E ICU   : Couldn't mmap '.../icudt63l.dat': Out of memory
+# The two free regions big enough (468 MB and 236 MB) sit below
+# TASK_UNMAPPED_BASE (0x40000000 on ARM), which neither the top-down walk nor
+# its bottom-up fallback reaches.
+# Read barriers are a compile-time choice - kUseReadBarrier forces
+# kCollectorTypeCC - so this cannot be switched with a property.
+# Note: it is PRODUCT_ART_USE_READ_BARRIER that Soong reads
+# (build/make/core/soong_config.mk:105 -> ArtUseReadBarrier); the same name
+# without the PRODUCT_ prefix in BoardConfig.mk is silently ignored.
+PRODUCT_ART_USE_READ_BARRIER := false
