+<!-- android.hardware.wifi (IWifi) DELIBERATELY ABSENT.
+
+     There is no working vendor HAL on this device and declaring one is worse
+     than declaring none.  Measured on 25 August:
+
+         android.hardware.wifi@1.0-service: finit_module return: -1:
+             Function not implemented
+         android.hardware.wifi@1.0-service: Failed to load WiFi driver
+         HalDevMgr: Cannot start IWifi: 9
+
+     libwifi-hal insists on inserting the driver itself and does it with
+     finit_module(2), which arrived in Linux 3.8.  This kernel is 3.4, so the
+     call can never succeed - and the driver is already loaded anyway, which
+     the HAL does not check.
+
+     With the entry gone, HalDeviceManager sees no IWifi in the manifest, logs
+     "Vendor Hal not supported, ignoring start" and returns true, and the
+     framework proceeds to wificond + supplicant.  AOSP's own documentation
+     says the vendor HAL "is optional (not required) for infrastructure
+     Station (STA) and Soft AP (SAP) modes to function".
+
